# Cloudflare Pages redirects & rewrites
#
# NOTE: this file does nothing on GitHub Pages, which is where the site is
# currently served from. It is kept for the Cloudflare deploy, and the rule below
# is deliberately commented out rather than deleted — see why.
#
# It used to rewrite /og.png to the dynamic renderer, on the premise that there
# was no static og.png file. There is one now: `scripts/render-og.mjs` bakes the
# same card to `og.png`, because a Pages Function cannot run on GitHub Pages and
# every homepage unfurl was 404ing on its own thumbnail as a result. Re-enabling
# this rewrite would shadow that real file with a request-time render that only
# works on one of the two hosts — so if it ever comes back, it comes back with a
# decision about which host is canonical, not by accident.
#
# /og.png /api/og-image?title=Pick%20a%20place.&subtitle=Leave%20the%20city.%20Weekend%20travel%20from%20Bangalore.&badge=Bangalore%20first 200
